worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_05_param_efficiency_claude/plan_param_efficiency.md:78:(A1, 2026-09-12 22:5x, from the Fable round-1 review, finding 4) §7 item 6's normalisation of fields absent from the historical M records reads `yaw_aug → 0`, `yaw_aug_seed → the run's seed` (the trainer resolves `None` to `args.seed`, so a literal `None` would make the type-strict diff refuse every run), `yaw_aug_width → 512`, `no_save → false`; a nonzero `yaw_aug` is refused outright. (A2, same time, from finding 1) The launcher's golden check ties the `--save-dir` arm root `ckpt/exp05/<tier>_<backbone>/` to the argv's `--backbone` and tier flags; a mismatch is refused before any directory is created. (A3, same time) Golden files are named `argv_golden_{S,L}_{simple,cylindrical}.txt` (one naming convention with the arm directories). (A4, same time, from observation 10) The L tier's fit at micro-batch 32 is at the edge of a 48 GB card (≈ 43.7 GiB extrapolated for one micro-batch step, TF32 on); the §7 fit probe for L runs on a completely free GPU, and §9's redesign branch (L at dim 640 if 32 × 2 does not fit) stays live until that probe passes. (A5, 2026-09-12 23:3x, from the Fable round-2 review, finding 3) §3's "exceeding the cumulative ceiling requires renewed authorisation" has a code path: `tools/exp04_launch.sh full --tier <t> … --renew-ceiling "<notebook entry timestamp>: <reason>"` records a `renewals` entry (timestamp, reason, old ceiling, new ceiling = 1.5 × the NEW clean receipt's T_run, receipt digest) in the arm's `cumulative_hours.json` and resets the ceiling to the new projection; without the flag the ceiling is `min(1.5 × T_run(receipt), recorded ceiling)` as implemented; every renewal is logged in the notebook before launch. (A6, same time, finding 4) The S/L evaluation launches bind the attempt's training completion (`--bind-input train_completion=ckpt/exp05/<arm>/final/completion.json`), and `tools/param_curve.py` admits an S/L run only if the run's `checkpoint_sha256` equals `train_completion.outputs['epoch_012.pth']` of the bound completion (the profile's literal epoch 12 is thereby machine-checked); the M arms are bound through the profile's pinned sha256 as before. (A7, 2026-09-12 23:5x, from the Fable round-3 review, finding 4) §5's generic "Cohorts (registered)" bullet is read as: a plotted curve point and its seed SD use the arm's own cohort (queries finite for all five seeds of that arm and metric); a comparison cell — including the fixed target of an H2 cell — uses the paired cohort (queries finite for all five seeds in both arms of the cell), the baseline's own-cohort mean being shown separately and labelled with both cohort sizes; this is the amended H2 rule the producer implements. (A8, same time, finding 1) The tier curve's single-delta contract is machine-checked: the producer admits an S/L run only with `train_manifest` and `train_completion` bound, requires the four new arms' training-launcher closure digests to equal each other and the approved `closures.training_launcher` pin, and checks the full §3 recipe keys (`num_shot, max_len, lr, weight_decay, decay_epochs, lr_gamma, epochs, batch_size, accum_steps, seed, tf32`) of the bound `args.json`. (A9, 2026-09-14 14:4x, from the Fable round-4 review, item 5) The approval record's `closures.training_launcher` is a LIST of approved training-launcher closure digests — `0bff0d4f…` (launch commit `f19b9b6`: S_simple, S_cylindrical, L_cylindrical) and `efde5a31…` (commit `f7b10b5`, round 4: receipt/arm binding and preflight ordering only; L_simple) — each reviewed; the producer requires every new arm's recorded launcher digest to be in the list and, as the single-delta check proper, the four arms' TRAINING closure digests (trainer + its imports, unchanged since `f19b9b6`) to be equal to each other and to the approved `closures.training` pin, and the §3 recipe dict to match type-strictly.
